## The Composite pattern in C#

The **Composite** pattern lets you treat individual objects (`Leaf`) and compositions of objects (`Composite`) uniformly.  
It’s the classic “tree” abstraction: a node may be a single item or a collection of items, but the client code can walk the structure without caring which kind it encounters.

Below is a full, idiomatic C# implementation followed by a quick “cook‑book” version that you can drop into any project.

---

## 1. Anatomy of the pattern

| Role | Purpose | Typical members |
|------|---------|-----------------|
| **Component** (interface/abstract base) | Declares the common interface for all objects in the composition. | `Add()`, `Remove()`, `GetChild()`, `Operation()` |
| **Leaf** | Represents an end‑node that has no children. | Implements `Operation()`. `Add()`/`Remove()` usually throw. |
| **Composite** | Represents a node that can hold child components. | Keeps a collection (`List<Component>`), implements `Add()`, `Remove()`, `GetChild()`, and forwards `Operation()` to children. |

> **Tip:** In C#, you can use an *abstract class* instead of an interface if you want to provide default (e.g. “NotSupported”) implementations of the mutating methods. This reduces boilerplate in the leaf classes.

---

## 2. A full example – a file system

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// 1. Component – the common abstraction
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
public abstract class FileSystemComponent
{
    public string Name { get; }

    protected FileSystemComponent(string name) => Name = name;

    // These are optional – Leaf will just throw
    public virtual void Add(FileSystemComponent child) =>
        throw new NotSupportedException($"{GetType().Name} does not support Add.");

    public virtual void Remove(FileSystemComponent child) =>
        throw new NotSupportedException($"{GetType().Name} does not support Remove.");

    public virtual FileSystemComponent GetChild(int index) =>
        throw new NotSupportedException($"{GetType().Name} does not support GetChild.");

    public abstract void Print(string indent = "");
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// 2. Leaf – a file
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
public sealed class File : FileSystemComponent
{
    public File(string name) : base(name) { }

    public override void Print(string indent = "")
    {
        Console.WriteLine($"{indent}File: {Name}");
    }
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// 3. Composite – a folder that can contain files and sub‑folders
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
public sealed class Folder : FileSystemComponent
{
    private readonly List<FileSystemComponent> _children = new();

    public Folder(string name) : base(name) { }

    public override void Add(FileSystemComponent child) => _children.Add(child);
    public override void Remove(FileSystemComponent child) => _children.Remove(child);
    public override FileSystemComponent GetChild(int index) => _children[index];

    public override void Print(string indent = "")
    {
        Console.WriteLine($"{indent}Folder: {Name}");
        foreach (var child in _children)
        {
            child.Print(indent + "  ");
        }
    }
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// 4. Client code
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        // Build a tree
        var root = new Folder("Root");

        var images = new Folder("Images");
        images.Add(new File("photo1.jpg"));
        images.Add(new File("photo2.png"));

        var docs = new Folder("Documents");
        docs.Add(new File("resume.docx"));
        docs.Add(new File("budget.xlsx"));

        root.Add(images);
        root.Add(docs);
        root.Add(new File("todo.txt"));

        // Treat everything uniformly
        root.Print();
    }
}
```

**Output**

```
Folder: Root
  Folder: Images
    File: photo1.jpg
    File: photo2.png
  Folder: Documents
    File: resume.docx
    File: budget.xlsx
  File: todo.txt
```

